## 12. Batch scanning queue

Every successfully captured identifier should appear in a batch review queue.

The queue should update while the camera is running.

Each item should show:
- Captured barcode.
- Identifier type.
- Book title, if found.
- Author, if found.
- Cover, if available.
- Lookup status.
- Duplicate status.

Use individual statuses:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Captured | Barcode decoded successfully |
| Searching | Metadata lookup in progress |
| Match found | Reliable metadata result available |
| No match | No reliable metadata result found |
| Invalid | Barcode failed validation |
| Duplicate | Possible existing or batch duplicate |
| Error | Lookup or processing error |

Do not make the entire batch fail because one barcode could not be identified.

### Metadata lookup behavior

Once a barcode has been captured:
- Start its metadata lookup independently.
- Allow other barcodes to be scanned at the same time.
- Use bounded concurrency for online lookup requests.
- Avoid overwhelming metadata providers.
- Preserve a separate result for every identifier.
- Handle provider timeouts and network errors.
- Allow failed lookups to be retried.

Do not wait until scanning is finished before starting every lookup.

However, camera scanning must never wait for metadata lookup to finish.

